criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

1. Black/African American race;
2. cisgender women;
3. aged 18-65 years;
4. currently under non-carceral correctional supervision in Alabama;
5. substance use in past 12 months;
6. HIV-negative or unknown status;
7. ≥1 HIV transmission risk factor in past 6 months (condomless sex, transactional sex, injection drug use, or STI diagnosis);
8. willing and able to participate in group sessions and follow-up assessments.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. known HIV-positive status;
2. pregnancy or intention to become pregnant within study period;
3. cognitive limitations interfering with informed consent or group participation;
4. current psychiatric crisis requiring immediate intervention;
5. scheduling conflicts that cannot be accommodated.
